  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nThrough the afternoon hours expect generally just some shower\nactivity. There are some breaks in the clouds near and south of the\nOhio River and therefore cannot rule out some thunderstorm activity\nlater in the day. There is a lot of model variability tonight and \nthrough this weekend with timing and strength of systems. There is a \nsignal that some thunderstorm activity will move through late in the\novernight hours and into the early morning daytime hours. Cannot \nrule out some small hail with these storms. There will then be a \nlull, followed by additional thunderstorms later in the day on \nSaturday and into Saturday night. There will be the potential for \ndamaging winds during this time. Also cannot rule out an isolated \ntornado, although damaging winds and heavy rain will be the primary \nthreats. There is a high potential for the need for an additional \nflood watch primarily near and north of I-70. Will hold off until \ntonight with uncertainty on axis of heaviest rainfall. Going into \nSunday there is the potential for additional heavy rain, damaging \nwinds, and the potential for an isolated tornado. Added severe \nwording into the HWO for Sunday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nWhile temperatures will warm for this weekend there is a lot of\nuncertainty in just how warm it will be as temperatures will be \nhighly dependent on thunderstorms and associated cloud cover. Made \nsome adjustments down with temperatures in spots. Still getting some \nlocations across the tri-state area reaching around 100 heat index \nfor Saturday and most of the area for Sunday. Will continue to \nmention heat potential for the weekend, but not confident enough to \nissue any headlines.",
